{'symbol': 'DE', 'date': '2019-11-27 14:30:00', 'title': 'DEERE SAYS FIRST PHASE OF EARLY ORDERS FOR COMBINES ARE DOWN DOUBLE-DIGITS- CONF CALL', 'text': "DEERE SAYS FIRST PHASE OF EARLY ORDERS FOR COMBINES WERE DOWN DOUBLE-DIGITS- CONF CALL.DEERE SAYS EARLY ORDERS FOR PLANTERS WERE UP SINGLE DIGITS- CONF CALL.DEERE SAYS EARLY ORDERS FOR SPRAYERS WERE DOWN LOW DOUBLE-DIGITS.DEERE SAYS UNCERTAINTY HAS SLOWED REPLACEMENT EQUIPMENT DEMAND IN 2019.DEERE SAYS SEEING SOME EVIDENCE THAT U.S. FARMER SENTIMENT IS BEGINNING TO IMPROVE.DEERE SAYS FLEET AGE IN THE U.S. HAS REACHED ITS HIGHEST POINT IN OVER A DECADE, AND CO'S 2020 OUTLOOK ANTICIPATES EVEN FURTHER AGING OF THIS FLEET.DEERE SAYS MANY U.S. CUSTOMERS WILL REACH A POINT  IN 2020 WHERE THEY SIMPLY NEED TO REPLACE THEIR EQUIPMENT.DEERE SAYS TRACTOR ORDER BOOK CURRENTLY EXTENDS THROUGH THE END OF MARCH, WELL AHEAD OF LAST YEAR.DEERE SAYS LEASE RETURN RATES REMAIN AT ELEVATED LEVELS.DEERE SAYS HAS TAKEN ACTIONS TO REDUCE CO'S MATURED LEASE INVENTORY.DEERE SAYS ANNOUNCED $140 MILLION VOLUNTARY SEPARATION PROGRAM FOR SALARIED EMPLOYEES.DEERE SAYS WILL REVIEW OVERSEAS FOOTPRINT.DEERE SAYS VOLUNTARY SEPARATION PROGRAM, COMBINED WITH INITIATIVES TAKEN IN 2019, IS ESTIMATED TO CONTRIBUTE TO ANNUALIZED SAVINGS OF ABOUT $150 MILLION.DEERE SAYS VOLUNTARY SEPARATION COSTS WILL BE INCURRED IN THE FIRST QUARTER OF FISCAL 2020."}
{'symbol': 'DE', 'date': '2019-11-27 09:30:00', 'title': 'DEERE & CO POSTS QTRLY EARNINGS PER SHARE OF $2.27', 'text': 'QTRLY EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.27.QTRLY ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.14.FULL-YEAR 2020 FORECAST CALLS FOR NET INCOME OF $2.7 TO $3.1 BILLION, REFLECTING UNCERTAINTIES IN OUR EQUIPMENT OPERATIONS..WORLDWIDE NET SALES AND REVENUES INCREASED 5 PERCENT IN FOURTH QUARTER TO $9.896 BILLION."JOHN DEERE’S PERFORMANCE REFLECTED CONTINUED UNCERTAINTIES IN THE AGRICULTURAL SECTOR".Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.13, REVENUE VIEW $8.53 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.NET INCOME IN Q4 WAS FAVORABLY AFFECTED BY DISCRETE ADJUSTMENTS TO PROVISION FOR INCOME TAXES.ADJUSTMENTS RELATED TO TAX REFORM WERE $41 MILLION IN Q4.DEERE- TRADE TENSIONS, DIFFICULT GROWING, HARVESTING CONDITIONS CAUSED MANY FARMERS TO BECOME CAUTIOUS ABOUT MAKING MAJOR INVESTMENTS IN NEW EQUIPMENT.WORLDWIDE SALES OF AGRICULTURE AND TURF EQUIPMENT ARE FORECAST TO DECLINE 5 TO 10 PERCENT FOR FISCAL-YEAR 2020.WORLDWIDE SALES OF CONSTRUCTION AND FORESTRY EQUIPMENT ARE ANTICIPATED TO BE DOWN 10 TO 15 PERCENT FOR 2020.DEERE - FAVOURABLE GENERAL ECONOMIC CONDITIONS SUPPORTED DEMAND FOR SMALLER EQUIPMENT, LED TO "SOLID RESULTS" FOR CONSTRUCTION AND FORESTRY BUSINESS.DEERE - DESPITE PRESENT CHALLENGES, THE LONGER-TERM OUTLOOK FOR OUR BUSINESSES REMAINS HEALTHY.AGRICULTURE & TURF NET SALES OF $5,756 MILLION , UP 3% IN QUARTER.DEERE’S WORLDWIDE SALES OF AGRICULTURE AND TURF EQUIPMENT ARE FORECAST TO DECLINE 5% TO 10% FOR FISCAL-YEAR 2020.'}
